          'First-time clients unfamiliar with chauffeured service in general sometimes default to point-to-point out of habit, since it maps most closely to how a rideshare trip works — worth remembering that the hourly option exists specifically because chauffeured service is built to handle a different kind of day than a single rideshare trip ever could.',
          'A simple test that resolves most borderline cases: ask yourself whether you would be upset if the vehicle left immediately after reaching the destination, with no ability to call it back for a quick second stop. If the answer is yes, that is a clear signal the day actually needs hourly flexibility rather than a single fixed trip, even if the original plan looked like a simple point-to-point ride on paper.',
